    <sys:String x:Key="Instance.Setup.Advanced.PreLaunchCommand.ToolTip">This does not override the global setting: the global command runs first, then the instance command. Executes a command or program before launching Minecraft, using Windows command prompt syntax. The following substitution tokens can be used for relative paths (paths end with \): · {path}: PCL executable folder · {minecraft}: .minecraft folder · {verpath}: Instance folder (.minecraft\versions\instance-name\) · {verindie}: Version folder when isolation is on, .minecraft folder otherwise · {java}: Java runtime folder Additionally, these tokens are also supported: · {user}: Player name · {login}: Player login method · {uuid}: Player UUID · {name}: Game instance name · {date}, {time}: Current system time · {version}: Game vanilla version Examples: · &quot;{verpath}test.exe&quot; : Run test.exe in the instance folder · &quot;{java}java.exe&quot; -jar &quot;{verpath}test.jar&quot; : Run test.jar from the instance folder with Java · notepad &quot;{verindie}options.txt&quot; : Open the instance settings file with Notepad Always wrap paths in double quotes to avoid failures caused by spaces.&#x0a;The working directory when executing the command is the current .minecraft folder.</sys:String>
